From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 06:00:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] sched/fair: Enable misfit_new_ns at 1 ms

A task that has not slept since its fork now counts as a misfit after
1 ms on a smaller CPU and moves to an idle big CPU at its spare
capacity. It can be switched off at run time without a rebuild: 0 in
/sys/kernel/debug/sched/misfit_new_ns.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 kernel/sched/fair.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/kernel/sched/fair.c b/kernel/sched/fair.c
index a2b8070fae..904435f76e 100644
--- a/kernel/sched/fair.c
+++ b/kernel/sched/fair.c
@@ -115,9 +115,9 @@ __read_mostly unsigned int sysctl_sched_fork_big_gap;
  * misfit_runtime_ns), and its first move to a CPU of the highest capacity
  * starts it at that CPU's spare capacity. A fork burst of short children
  * never reaches it; a CPU-bound new thread gets the big CPU within it.
- * (default: 0 = off, units: nanoseconds)
+ * (default: 1 msec, 0 = off, units: nanoseconds)
  */
-__read_mostly unsigned int sysctl_sched_misfit_new;
+__read_mostly unsigned int sysctl_sched_misfit_new	= 1000000UL;
 
 static int __init setup_sched_thermal_decay_shift(char *str)
 {
-- 
2.43.0

